@model ChooseOrganisationViewModel
@*
    "Which organisation?" — the step between Add on a grouped list and the Create form. Slice F6c.

    WHY THIS EXISTS. An "All <plural>" list groups every dimension type that shares a name, and the
    demo tenant has two Position types — one per company, prefixed for the reason ADR-0028 gives.
    The list is therefore about no single type, and Add posted an empty dimensionTypeId: the Create
    form could not know what it was creating, and the reader got a 404 from a button the screen had
    just offered them.

    REFUSING TO GUESS IS THE PRODUCT'S HABIT HERE, not a new idea: the tree view asks the same
    question when it has no structure to draw. Picking one of the two would silently create a
    Crescent position from Zenith's list half the time.

    LINKS, NOT A FORM. Nothing is written by choosing; this only decides which Create form to open,
    and a GET keeps the back button working the way it does everywhere else on these screens.
*@
<h1 id="choose-organisation-heading">@T["Add to {0}", Model.Caption]</h1>

<p class="text-muted" id="choose-organisation-hint">
    @T["More than one organisation has a dimension of this name. Which one is this for?"]
</p>

<div class="list-group mb-3" id="choose-organisation-choices">
    @foreach (var choice in Model.Choices)
    {
        <a class="list-group-item list-group-item-action choose-organisation-choice"
           data-dimension-type-id="@choice.DimensionTypeId"
           asp-action="Create"
           asp-route-dimensionTypeId="@choice.DimensionTypeId"
           asp-route-group="@Model.Group"
           asp-route-structureId="@Model.StructureId">@choice.Organisation</a>
    }
</div>

<a class="btn btn-link" id="choose-organisation-cancel"
   asp-action="Index"
   asp-route-group="@Model.Group"
   asp-route-structureId="@Model.StructureId">@T["Cancel"]</a>
